  "content": {
    "id": "p43-q44-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "44",
    "prompt": "Find the value of $$(1-\\alpha)(1-\\beta)(1-\\gamma)$$ if $\\alpha$, $\\beta$ and $\\gamma$ are the roots of $2x^3-3x^2+x+7=0$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{7}{2}$.",
      "worked": "The root-coefficient relationships give\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma&=\\frac32\\\\\\alpha\\beta+\\alpha\\gamma+\\beta\\gamma&=\\frac12\\\\\\alpha\\beta\\gamma&=-\\frac72.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}(1-\\alpha)(1-\\beta)(1-\\gamma)&=1-(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)+(\\alpha\\beta+\\alpha\\gamma+\\beta\\gamma)-\\alpha\\beta\\gamma\\\\(1-\\alpha)(1-\\beta)(1-\\gamma)&=1-\\frac32+\\frac12-\\left(-\\frac72\\right)\\\\(1-\\alpha)(1-\\beta)(1-\\gamma)&=\\frac72.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 72
  },
